# Source manifest — reproducible-by-reference (Invariant 3).
# Re-clone at build time; the working tree under sources/typos/ is gitignored.
#
# TOOLCHAIN SOURCE — a tool this repo actually RUNS (#81, ingested 2026-08-02).
#
# ⚠️ INVARIANT: this pin MUST track the version we actually run.
#   version source: mise.toml `[tools] typos`
#   pinned here:    1.48.0
# A pin that drifts from the installed version makes the corpus answer questions
# about code we are not running. Not hypothetical — `sources/graphify.manifest`
# records exactly that failure: it sat two releases behind for weeks, so every
# "how does graphify work?" answer came from the wrong source.
#
# Pin the RELEASE TAG, never a branch head — a branch drifts ahead of the release.
# ⚠️ THIS TAG IS ANNOTATED. Do NOT use `--refs` — it strips the peeled line,
# and a bump recorded from it pins the TAG OBJECT, not the commit `kb-build`
# checks out (#500). To bump: change the version in its source above, then
#   git ls-remote --tags https://github.com/crate-ci/typos <version> '<version>^{}'
# and set ref/commit here to the `^{}` (peeled) line's SHA — NOT the bare
# `<version>` line — then `mise run kb-build`.
#
# kind = code: AST extraction only, no LLM, no cost. NOTE this extracts the
# SOURCE and skips every .md by design — the tool's DOCS are a separate
# `kind = docs` mirror (#123), not this manifest.
url = https://github.com/crate-ci/typos
ref = v1.50.0
commit = 4d9c206a77c041268485162b8e2579ad7a5cb9a3
kind = code
added = 2026-08-02
